{"chunk_id": "30d8b565ba2d", "text": "Draupadi recounts to Bhima the humiliation inflicted by Kichaka, who assaulted and kicked her publicly while King Virata and others failed to intervene. She fears continued harassment and declares she would rather die than submit to him, urging Bhima to avenge the insult. Bhima promises vengeance but insists it must be done secretly to preserve the Pandavas\u2019 disguise during their exile. Draupadi tricks the lustful Kichaka into agreeing to a secret nighttime meeting in the deserted dancing hall. Believing he is going to a tryst, Kichaka arrives adorned for love, only to encounter Bhima lying in wait. A brutal hand\u2011to\u2011hand struggle follows, shaking the hall, until Bhima overpowers and crushes him, killing the tyrant who had tormented Draupadi.\nDraupadi persuades Bhima to avenge Kichaka\u2019s assault, lures Kichaka to a nighttime tryst, and Bhima secretly kills him in a brutal wrestling fight.\nThemes: revenge for dishonor, sexual predation, secret justice, loyalty between spouses, disguise and strategy", "vector": [-0.007990824989974499, -0.011307256296277046, 0.004885935690253973, -0.007158305495977402, -0.0013699044939130545, 0.042827002704143524, -0.0151491304859519, -0.005742339417338371, 0.0062609585002064705, -0.03218166530132294, 0.010017532855272293, 0.01512183528393507, 0.028633221983909607, -0.006469088140875101, 0.0006943351472727954, 0.01946185529232025, 0.05060628429055214, 0.013729752972722054, 0.03826861456036568, -0.02170010656118393, 0.004387788940221071, 0.008727810345590115, 0.009737752377986908, 0.02578081749379635, -0.039223965257406235, 0.009621744975447655, 0.012651571072638035, -0.022600864991545677, 0.017360085621476173, -0.010672630742192268, -0.019257137551903725, -0.007936233654618263, 0.005755987484008074, -0.000343755615176633, -0.03665816783905029, -0.006452028173953295, -0.01588611491024494, -0.02255992218852043, 0.004073888063430786, 0.011034299619495869, 0.002738103037700057, -0.0